# Normalise line endings in the repository, but check .bat files out as CRLF.
#
# Windows batch files are much happier with CRLF, and the ones here are written
# that way deliberately. Without an explicit rule git would normalise them to LF
# in the repository and then hand back whatever the local setting says, so a
# contributor with core.autocrlf=false could end up with a .bat that behaves
# oddly. Everything else stays LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary-ish assets, just in case one is ever added
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.onnx binary
*.tflite binary
